  "academy-qf-20-warning-lights.html": {
    "file": "academy-qf-20-warning-lights.html",
    "subtitle": "What every common light means, how urgent it is, and what to check before calling anyone.",
    "time": "15 minutes to learn",
    "level": "Beginner",
    "intro": "Dash lights follow a color code: red means stop or act now, yellow/amber means check soon, green or blue is just information. Knowing the handful that matter keeps you safe and stops you paying for checks you can do yourself.",
    "save": [
      {
        "label": "A shop charges",
        "value": "$100+ just to look"
      },
      {
        "label": "You'll spend",
        "value": "$0"
      }
    ],
    "learn": [
      "The red lights that mean stop",
      "The amber lights that mean check soon",
      "The first checks for each",
      "When it's safe to keep driving"
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "label": "Step 1",
        "title": "Red: act now"
      },
      {
        "label": "Step 2",
        "title": "Amber: check soon"
      },
      {
        "label": "Step 3",
        "title": "Information"
      }
    ],
    "firstStep": {
      "label": "Step 1",
      "title": "Red: act now",
      "items": [
        "Oil pressure (oil can): stop, engine off, check the oil level. Don't restart if it's low or the light stays on.",
        "Temperature (thermometer): stop and let it cool. Check coolant only when cold. Turning on the heater full can shed heat on the way to a safe stop.",
        "Brake (!) or BRAKE: check the parking brake is fully off. If it is, check brake fluid; a soft pedal means don't drive.",
        "Battery/charging: the alternator isn't charging. You have limited time before the car dies. Turn off accessories and head to a safe place."
      ],
      "notes": []
    }
  },
